{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794232794,"nonce":"hsnzMFtJ7oBdiUxYXb9M49E4o78=","title":"Upgrading the demo from sha-731bc42 to v0.3.0 on 2026-11-09 took three manual steps that the documented entry point (`just stack up demo-oracle \u003cref\u003e`) does not cover.","message":"1. **The box has no `just`.** bootstrap.sh installs k3s and README says to install helm, but nothing installs just ≥1.43. So the recipe cannot run on the only host it allows. The upgrade ran `deploy/demo-oracle/deploy.sh 0.3.0` directly, with the same env the recipe sets: IMAGE_REPOSITORY, IMAGE_PULL_POLICY=Always, and SCARAB_CLONE/SIDECAR/WSFETCH_IMAGE set to `:\u003cref\u003e`. Either bootstrap.sh installs just, or README documents the direct call.\n2. **The StatefulSet orphan-delete.** The box's `scarab-workspace` StatefulSet still carried chart-0.1.0 labels in volumeClaimTemplates. The one-time `kubectl delete sts --cascade=orphan …` from the chart README (\"Upgrading from 0.2.1 or earlier\") had to be run by hand. deploy.sh could detect version labels on the existing template and do it.\n3. **A pre-upgrade backup.** I took one with `kubectl create job --from=cronjob/scarab-postgres-backup pre-030-\u003cts\u003e`. It wrote `s3://demo-scarab/pg/scarab-1.dump`, which looks like a rotating slot. So a pre-upgrade dump can overwrite a nightly one. deploy.sh could take a dump under its own key before `helm upgrade`.\n\nThe upgrade itself succeeded:\n- `/healthz` and `/readyz` return 200.\n- `/v1/auth/login` redirects to GitHub.\n- The server and Depot run `scarab-server:0.3.0`.\n- No errors appeared in the server log after the rollout.","files":null}]}